From: OE-Alliance contributors
Subject: [PATCH] STB: identify hardware-managed video in player information

The STB codec uses an opaque hardware video plane and leaves deinterlacing
to the platform driver. Populate the process-information labels instead of
leaving them unknown, without claiming a particular pixel layout or active
deinterlacing algorithm. Keep the internal picture format unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [STB-specific player integration]

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecSTB.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecSTB.cpp
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecSTB.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecSTB.cpp
@@ -437,6 +437,8 @@ bool CDVDVideoCodecSTB::Open(CDVDStreamInfo& hints, CDVDCodecOptions& options)
   m_processInfo.SetVideoDAR(hints.aspect > 0.0 ? static_cast<float>(hints.aspect)
                                                : static_cast<float>(hints.width) / hints.height);
   m_processInfo.SetVideoInterlaced(hints.interlaced);
+  m_processInfo.SetVideoPixelFormat("STB hardware");
+  m_processInfo.SetVideoDeintMethod("STB driver-managed");
   m_open = true;
   m_failed = false;
   CLog::Log(LOGINFO, "CDVDVideoCodecSTB: using backend '{}' for codec {}", m_session->BackendName(),
